  "agent": {
    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/wireframe/base/v2` \"Wireframe v2\"** (gate 29 — WIREFRAME pack opener; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Core tier, tags wireframe + docs-only (the Developer/Docs facet). THE m0 visualization primitive: the Layout page renders through it, the perf heatmap paints through it (`cellColors`), every sandbox wireframe still is one. Props = pure defaults (`F`) so Make opens on the **NEW COVER** first, then renders the bare single cell.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | core · not internal · not deprecated · not primitive | confirm — chart note says \"consider internal:true\"; recommend **NO** (people trace layouts with it; Layout page + facet depend on browse) |\n| Label | \"Wireframe v2\" | \"Wireframe\"? (v1 is deprecated-hidden, so the suffix reads odd in browse) — untouched, your call |\n| Cover | none → **pane cover ADDED**: 3 bubbles (string / labels / trace) + hero = its OWN render of a 6-cell editorial, ink on the theme surface, inlined flat, sized to the hero box | keep / band / strike |\n| Tutorial | none | skip? (the cover bubbles carry the mental model) |\n| Previews | `preview.png` only (07-15 regen) — default look UNCHANGED | leave as-is; eyeball ☐ |\n| Battery | **32/32 GREEN** (25 CLI renders + pixel asserts) | — |\n| E2E | basic tier 6/6 (default + 5 paint-order variants) | — |\n\n**Pre-audit findings → fixed:**\n\n| Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `grid-paper` preset + `theme.paperGrid` resolved a lattice that NOTHING drew — the Layout page sells it as \"Textbook — hand-drawn paper grid\" (audit-every-knob) | **wired**: ONE masked ink tile as a full-canvas top overlay (`X` → `X{1}`, nests past a root overlay), pitch 1/16 short side, alpha 0.08 — `utils/paperGrid.ts` + 9 locks. Revertable to a PRUNE (preset + Layout \"Textbook\" entry) if you'd rather |\n| Schema: labelContent \"Default aspect\", labels \"dimensions and aspect ratio are rendered\" — the real default is number + W×H | descriptions corrected |\n| Description was engineering-speak (\"masked color tile… no per-cell drawtext\") | user-facing blurb (what it draws, transparent default, trace, presets) |\n| No `format` on the doc (pre-gate-26 template) | `format:{image,png,rgba}` authored (same values the hints seeded; `-o .mp4` still refuses loudly — verified) |\n| `labelsByStableKey` / `cellColors` = programmatic props in the human form | `consumer:\"agent\"` → tucked under Agent props |\n\n**Verified, no change needed:** transparent default (alpha coverage 2.2%) · white+fill opaque · null tiles empty · label ladder degrade/hide/number-floor at 80×90px cells · overlay label suppression (per-line rects) · long custom labels shrink-to-fit · stableKey labels · heat cells (nested `F{F}` + flat) · trace backgroundImage contain/opacity · **400 inline masks render in 17s — no argv cliff** (100 → 4.6s, 200 → 9.6s, linear).\n\n**Design notes (not bugs):** cell bodies are transparent, so an overlay's label sits over the base tiles' borders; an infeasible string (60 cols @ 320px) renders 5px stripes with no error card — the wireframe shows what the engine would do.\n\nUnit 101/101 (wireframe family incl. 16 new locks). Stress ×10 pre-minted in `stress/` (agent pass clean) — review after the default verdict.",
